def table(x):return x.round(3).to_html(index=False)
x=d.copy()
for col in x.columns:
 if col not in ['dataset','policy']:x[col]*=100
html='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Logistic selectors across ten datasets</title><style>body{font:17px system-ui;line-height:1.55;color:#19283b;max-width:1200px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:7px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:right}th{background:#edf3f8}img{width:100%}.note{padding:18px;background:#edf3f8;border-radius:10px}</style></head><body><h1>Logistic selectors: training coverage and all ten datasets</h1><p>The existing logistic experiment already trained and evaluated across all ten datasets. This report breaks out the frozen results; it does not retrain or select anything using test performance.</p><div class="note">There are25,000 validation contexts:500 per backbone/dataset combination. At fixed50, the ten judge-specific classifiers together receive21,365 disagreement training pairs:14,981 favour NN and6,384 favour control. These pairs cover9,590 distinct backbone–target contexts and7,493 distinct target texts. They are not21,365 independent texts. Each judge has391–6,189 informative training examples. All eligible validation cases, including unchanged decisions, remain in cutoff selection.</div><p>One model per judge pools its available training disagreements across five backbones and ten datasets. The per-combination inclusion cutoff is selected using grouped out-of-fold validation predictions. Final models are fitted to all their validation disagreements. These are held-out examples within the ten known datasets, not a study of transfer to an unseen dataset. Original API missingness is retained.</p><img src="dataset_deltas.png"><h2>Fixed50 test performance</h2><p>Percentages; each dataset averages50 backbone/judge combinations. Delta columns are percentage points. Results use each judge's validation-selected logistic regularization and inclusion cutoff.</p>'''+table(x[x.policy=='fixed50'].drop(columns='policy'))+'''<h2>Shared tuned threshold performance</h2><p>Average of the three shared-threshold anchor settings, keeping each probe/judge pair identical across the competing explanation-selection methods.</p>'''+table(x[x.policy=='anchor_average'].drop(columns='policy'))+'''<h2>Training data per judge: fixed50</h2><p>validation_rows is the eligible paired pool. training_flips are the examples actually used to fit the classifier; training_helpful is the include-explanation class.</p>'''+table(j)+'''<h2>Training coverage per dataset: fixed50</h2><p>Training pairs are summed across the ten original outcome judges. Unique contexts and target texts remove those repeated counts. Every dataset contributes2,500 validation and2,500 test contexts before API missingness.</p>'''+table(n)+'''<p>The strongest fixed50 improvement over always-NN is RAGTruth (+2.52 F1 points), followed by High Stakes (+1.87). Gains are not universal: FAVA and HaluEval change very slightly downward. Relative to cosine filtering, logistic improves the fixed50 dataset average for all ten. After shared threshold tuning, additional gains are much smaller and not uniform.</p><p>These are descriptive results on the previously inspected test set, without refitting uncertainty intervals. The original selection audit, saved models and full methods remain in the <a href="../../nn_learned_gate_20261019/results/report.html">main logistic/tree report</a>.</p><ul>'''+''.join('<li><a href="'+f+'">'+f+'</a></li>' for f in ['dataset_performance.csv','training_by_judge.csv','training_by_dataset.csv','COMPLETED.json','dataset_deltas.pdf'])+'</ul></body></html>'
